{
    "background_story": "Jonas was a charismatic food cart vendor who had been serving the best Coney Islands in the city for over a decade. His cart, 'Jonas' Classic Coneys', was a staple on the corner of 5th and Main, attracting locals and tourists alike. Jonas took pride in his secret recipe, passed down from his Greek immigrant grandfather, which featured a perfect balance of savory flavors and spices. As the years went by, Jonas became a beloved fixture in the community, always ready with a warm smile and a steaming hot Coney. His loyalty to his customers and his craft earned him a reputation as the 'Coney King', with people coming from all over to taste his delicious creations.",
